# One of the four roles from SP-A02-1. Which one a node takes is the boot value `role`, read from
# a credential by workpod-role-generator; the image is the same artifact either way (AB-A02-1).
#
# `work` runs the pods. It is the role that scales — SP-A02-1's "scaling means: add nodes with
# role = work" — and the one SP-A02-5 updates without a drain command: the worker stops pulling,
# runs its open leases to completion, restarts and enrolls again.
#
# The sequence here ends at the worker, whose registration against a remote control plane needs
# the certificate name of contract/identity.md — enrollment, AP-6.1. Until then a lone work node
# runs its sequence to the selftest and refuses the plaintext hop, by name.

[Unit]
Description=Workpod node role: work
Documentation=https://github.com/Cheety/warft/blob/main/01-specification.md
Wants=workpod-work.slice
Wants=workpod-disk.service workpod-selftest.service workpod-worker.service
# SP-B02-2: the egress proxy stands on the work node, not centrally. It is a unit of this role and
# of no other — one gate per work node is what makes it not a central throughput bottleneck.
Wants=workpod-egress-gate.service
